// Feature: build a warband. Code: routes ((app)/warbands/**; api/v1/warbands; uploads/fighters), services/warbands, lib/warbands.
views {
  dynamic view warband_build {
    title 'Build a warband'
    description '''
      **A player builds a warband like the Trench Companion builder, by the books: faction (with its variant or Sin), name and
      starting banks; then fighters and their kit on a two-column page, checked on every change; the Arsenal, campaign data
      and play mode; then assigns it to their campaign seat.**

      **Decisions**
      - The player owns the warband; it sits in at most one campaign at a time (seats.warband_id is unique).
      - Every change runs the warband engine; a refused change says why. A campaign whose CM allows going beyond
        limits turns refusals into warnings for warbands in it; outside a campaign the warband's own "ignore limits"
        switch does the same (revision 2, R9).
      - Groups: Elites, Troops, Mercenaries, Special; the Dead list shows fighters whose status is dead. Each fighter has
        an image slot (empty by default; PNG, JPEG or WebP up to 2 MB, checked by file signature, in the uploads volume).
      - Add fighter per group offers the entry's upgrades and loadouts and shows "n / max"; the engine checks them with
        the recruit, as one purchase. The equip picker shows used / max, counting copies held in the Arsenal.
      - Kit moves fighter to fighter and to and from the Arsenal. Sell gives half the price back, rounded up, in the
        item's own currency; refund (full price) and fighter refund only while games played is 0 (a Trench Companion
        convenience). Delete gives nothing back.
      - Fighter campaign data is entered by hand: status (active, misses next game, captured, unfit, retired, dead),
        experience with the advancement marks, battle scars (unfit at 3), advancements picked from the skill tables,
        injuries from the trauma table, promote and demote (no more than 6 elites). Unfit sends the kit to the Arsenal.
      - Threshold and field strength follow games played (Papal States 200 lower). The patron may change until the
        first game, then only by the CM (R8). The Court's Sin is a dedication on the warband (R2).
      - Play mode shows read-only fighter cards with full profiles and keyword pop-ups; print uses a print stylesheet.
      - A campaign keeps one rules version: the CM cannot change it while a seated warband uses other rules.
      - Export as Trench Companion text and JSON; import Trench Companion text and JSON.
      - The Arsenal, fireteams and locations are typed JSONB on the warband (the engine's own shapes); fighters are
        rows, in roster order (prices depend on it). Buying takes the worth it adds from the banks.
    '''
    user -> fl.app.web.areas 'new warband, add fighter, equip, move, sell, campaign data, play'
    fl.app.web.areas -> fl.app.services.warbandService 'create / recruit / equip / move / sell / refund / status / xp'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.services.rulesService 'the warband\'s rules set'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.warbandEngine 'check the change, sell value, refund window, progression'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.repos 'save with a version check'
    fl.app.repos -> fl.app.warbandTables 'warbands, fighters, Arsenal'
    user -> fl.app.web.areas 'assign to my seat'
    fl.app.web.areas -> fl.app.services.warbandService 'assignToSeat'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.services.campaignService 'my seat, allow beyond limits, CM for the patron'
    fl.app.services.warbandService -> fl.app.services.auditService 'record warband.assigned'
  }
}
